│ medications", "abstract": "The psychopharmacology of depression is a field that has evolved rapidly in just under 5  │
│ decades. Early antidepressant medications—tricyclic antidepressants (TCAs) and monoamine oxidase inhibitors          │
│ (MAOIs)—were discovered through astute clinical observations. These first-generation medications were effective      │
